  "title": "Quiddities",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "c15d011f-60b0-4f59-a165-efcabbc826d1",
      "text": "Quiddities are the properties that underlie the structure and dynamics physics describes. They categorically ground the most basic physical dispositions, the way a ball’s spherical shape grounds its disposition to roll. They are also called inscrutables.",
